-specific powder XRD facts; no phase transfer to controls","supporting_information":"Matching local SI, all 19 pages included"},"protocol_art":{"record_id":"larson2023-inp-edta-chemmater3c01309-postsynthetic-edta","bindings":[{"operation_id":"prepare-slurry","asset_path":"assets/protocol/larson2023-inp-edta-chemmater3c01309-op-5ad4f62b54e7.svg","asset_sha256":"f6212fc0c2cf792efd0e9715fcf69c23c567e52e5e619ea299e79ba3de3b7723","caption":"Mix 0.15 mmol EDTA with 0.6 mL anhydrous oleylamine to make a slurry. Conceptual operation diagram; only source-stated equipment and conditions apply.","source_locator":"Main PDF p.7, Postsynthesis Addition of EDTA; SI p.15 Figure S16","mode":"source-operation"},{"operation_id":"add-after-growth","asset_path":"assets/protocol/larson2023-inp-edta-chemmater3c01309-op-e9b878daa5f3.svg","asset_sha256":"e0ab12085f2be99ed492b464d12d9fdba1f82033e8c2daacf7f0d5ecfcf05323","caption":"After the EDTA-free baseline reaction has grown for 2 h, inject the EDTA/oleylamine slurry. Continue the source reaction; this is not EDTA present during initial nucleation. Conceptual operation diagram; only source-stated equipment and conditions apply.","source_locator":"Main PDF p.7, Postsynthesis Addition of EDTA; SI p.15 Figure S16","mode":"source-operation"},{"operation_id":"monitor-post","asset_path":"assets/protocol/larson2023-inp-edta-chemmater3c01309-op-c8becef5ef38.svg","asset_sha256":"feb669f4968d9429ba321cde7ec35e801082cf399d2294e2248f821caa3e7438","caption":"Use 20 µL reaction aliquots in 2 mL toluene. The spectrum reaches a plateau after 1 h following addition. Conceptual operation diagram; only source-stated equipment and conditions apply.","source_locator":"Main PDF p.7, Postsynthesis Addition of EDTA; SI p.15 Figure S16","mode":"analytical-measurement"},{"operation_id":"purify-post","asset_path":"assets/protocol/larson2023-inp-edta-chemmater3c01309-op-4c5884d5e883.svg","asset_sha256":"8ed9944a4c317510be4aed8a41d5e11cc2e0c1fa7c0fb4723fb07e3a91798fb7","caption":"Cool to room temperature and move into the nitrogen glovebox; precipitate with anhydrous methanol, centrifuge at 7830 rpm for 10 min, redisperse in toluene. The source standard procedure says repeated 3 times, with total cycle counting ambiguous. Conceptual operation diagram; only source-stated equipment and conditions apply.","source_locator":"Main PDF p.7 / printed 6158, General Considerations and Synthesis of InP Quantum Dots; Main PDF p.7, Postsynthesis Addition of EDTA; SI p.15 Figure S16","mode":"source-operation"}]},"presentation_status":"pending","general_background":[{"id":"general-context","title":"Thermodynamics and kinetics","summary":"Thermodynamics describes which states are energetically favoured, while kinetics governs how quickly a system can move between them. A change can be favourable yet proceed slowly when an activation barrier or limited transport restricts the pathway.","label":"General background, not the authors' interpretation","reference":{"doi":"10.1021/cr400544s","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/cr400544s","kind":"review","title":"Mechanisms of Nucleation and Growth of Nanoparticles in Solution","container":"Chemical Reviews","year":2014}}]}
